<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S6" title="6 Theoretical Analysis on Context-Conditional Masked Modeling ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Modeling the Joint Conditional with Random Masks ‣ 6 Theoretical Analysis on Context-Conditional Masked Modeling ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Formal Version of <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 6.1 (Informal; See ). ‣ 6.1 Modeling the Joint Conditional with Random Masks ‣ 6 Theoretical Analysis on Context-Conditional Masked Modeling ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> has a strictly positive probability density function.
Then there is a one-to-one correspondence between the distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the family of conditionals <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\forall\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\forall\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is clear that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> directly yields all conditionals <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show the converse: <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be recovered from this family of conditionals.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">As the first step, we derive <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, select a mask <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=\frac{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi\setminus\{j\}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}=\frac{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{\int_{\Omega}p\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi\setminus\{j\}},{X^{\text{te}}_{j}}^{\prime}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\mathrm{d}{X^{\text{te}}_{j}}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=\frac{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi\setminus\{j\}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}=\frac{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{\int_{\Omega}p\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi\setminus\{j\}},{X^{\text{te}}_{j}}^{\prime}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\mathrm{d}{X^{\text{te}}_{j}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each term on the right-hand side belongs to <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> can indeed be recovered.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now use induction to show that the knowledge of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}</annotation></semantics></math> suffices to recover all conditionals in</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{k}=\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):|\pi|=k\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{k}=\{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):|\pi|=k\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):j\in[d]\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtainable for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\in{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\in{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\pi|=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\pi|=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Pick <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=\pi\setminus\{j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=\pi\setminus\{j\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\Omega}\frac{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|X^{\text{te}}_{j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\,\mathrm{d}X^{\text{te}}_{j}=\int_{\Omega}\frac{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\,\mathrm{d}X^{\text{te}}_{j}=\frac{1}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\Omega}\frac{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|X^{\text{te}}_{j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\,\mathrm{d}X^{\text{te}}_{j}=\int_{\Omega}\frac{p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\,\mathrm{d}X^{\text{te}}_{j}=\frac{1}{p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Each term on the left-hand side belongs to <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> is obtainable. Finally,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\cdot p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\cdot p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi^{\prime}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">showing that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained as well. Hence, any element in <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained. By induction, the claim follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we show that the knowledge of a single conditional distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{j}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-j},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., when <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi=\{j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi=\{j\}</annotation></semantics></math>) is insufficient to recover the full conditional distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmexample1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmexample1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmexample1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmexample1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., a setting with no in-context samples and a feature dimension of <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the target distribution <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose further that <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\sim{\mathcal{N}}(\bm{\mu},\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\sim{\mathcal{N}}(\bm{\mu},\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}=(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}=(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\begin{pmatrix}\Sigma_{11}&amp;\Sigma_{12}\\
\Sigma_{21}&amp;\Sigma_{22}\end{pmatrix}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\begin{pmatrix}\Sigma_{11}&amp;\Sigma_{12}\\
\Sigma_{21}&amp;\Sigma_{22}\end{pmatrix}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the conditional distribution of <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\text{te}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\text{te}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\text{te}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\text{te}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\text{te}}_{1}\mid X^{\text{te}}_{2}\sim{\mathcal{N}}\left(\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}X^{\text{te}}_{2}+\mu_{1}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\mu_{2},\Sigma_{11}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\Sigma_{21}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\text{te}}_{1}\mid X^{\text{te}}_{2}\sim{\mathcal{N}}\left(\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}X^{\text{te}}_{2}+\mu_{1}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\mu_{2},\Sigma_{11}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\Sigma_{21}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, knowledge of <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{1}|X^{\text{te}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{1}|X^{\text{te}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> alone provides access only to the quantities <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{11}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\Sigma_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{11}-\Sigma_{12}\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\Sigma_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>. These are insufficient to uniquely determine the full parameter set <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mu},\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mu},\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be fully recovered from <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{1}|X^{\text{te}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{1}|X^{\text{te}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> alone. By symmetry, <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})</annotation></semantics></math> also cannot be recovered solely from <math id="A2.Thmexample1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X^{\text{te}}_{2}|X^{\text{te}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X^{\text{te}}_{2}|X^{\text{te}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2 The Choice of Mask Number ‣ 6 Theoretical Analysis on Context-Conditional Masked Modeling ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}),\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}),\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> the distribution induced by the learned family of conditional probabilities <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}):\pi\in\Pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We overload the notation by writing <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})\coloneqq q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})\coloneqq q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Sample Efficiency</h4>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Formal Version of <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 6.2 (Informal; see ). ‣ Sample efficiency. ‣ 6.2 The Choice of Mask Number ‣ 6 Theoretical Analysis on Context-Conditional Masked Modeling ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose there exists <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})=p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\in\Omega^{m\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\in\Omega^{m\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\in\Omega^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\in\Omega^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\subseteq[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\subseteq[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, and that the minimizer of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is unique for every <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\in\Omega^{m\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\in\Omega^{m\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\in\Omega^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}\in\Omega^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\subseteq[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\subseteq[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient norm <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla_{\theta}q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla_{\theta}q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Hessian norm <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla^{2}_{\theta}q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla^{2}_{\theta}q_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> exist and are finite. Assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L_{k}(\theta^{*})\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L_{k}(\theta^{*})\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every sufficiently small neighborhood <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a sufficiently large <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{k,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{k,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique minimizer of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}_{k}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}_{k}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}(\hat{\theta}_{k,n}-\theta^{*})\xrightarrow{d}{\mathcal{N}}(0,\Gamma_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}(\hat{\theta}_{k,n}-\theta^{*})\xrightarrow{d}{\mathcal{N}}(0,\Gamma_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k+1}\preceq\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k+1}\preceq\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Formal Version of ). ‣ B.2.1 Sample Efficiency ‣ B.2 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details in ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> is based on the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">Van der Vaart (2000)</a></cite>, Theorem 5.23; statement adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qin &amp; Risteski (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024c)</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a loss <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:\Theta\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:\Theta\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the the set of global minima of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{*}=\{\theta^{*}:L(\theta^{*})=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}L(\theta)\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{*}=\{\theta^{*}:L(\theta^{*})=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}L(\theta)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the following conditions are met:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Gradient bounds on </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) The map </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\mapsto\ell_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\mapsto\ell_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is measurable and differentiable at every </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-almost every </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Furthermore, there exists a function </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, s.t. </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[B(\mathbf{X})^{2}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[B(\mathbf{X})^{2}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and and for every </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1},\theta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1},\theta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> near </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\ell_{\theta_{1}}(\mathbf{X})-\ell_{\theta_{2}}(\mathbf{X})\right|&lt;B(\mathbf{X})\left\lVert\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\right\rVert_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\ell_{\theta_{1}}(\mathbf{X})-\ell_{\theta_{2}}(\mathbf{X})\right|&lt;B(\mathbf{X})\left\lVert\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Twice-differentiability of </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is twice-differentiable at every </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with Hessian </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and furthermore </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L(\theta^{*})\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{\theta}L(\theta^{*})\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Uniform law of large numbers) The loss </span><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies a uniform law of large numbers, that is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\left|\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]-L(\theta)\right|\xrightarrow{p}0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\left|\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]-L(\theta)\right|\xrightarrow{p}0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Realizability) The data distribution </span><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies: </span><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\theta^{*}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\theta^{*}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta^{*}}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{*}}=p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for every <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and every sufficiently small neighborhood <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a sufficiently large <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that there is a unique minimizer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\ell_{\theta}(\mathbf{X})]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\left(\hat{\theta}_{n}-\theta^{*}\right)\xrightarrow{d}{\mathcal{N}}\left(0,\left(\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L\left(\theta^{*}\right)\right)^{-1}\operatorname{Cov}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L\left(\theta^{*}\right)\right)^{-1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\left(\hat{\theta}_{n}-\theta^{*}\right)\xrightarrow{d}{\mathcal{N}}\left(0,\left(\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L\left(\theta^{*}\right)\right)^{-1}\operatorname{Cov}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L\left(\theta^{*}\right)\right)^{-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to Lemma 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024c)</a></cite>, we have the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same assumptions as in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Formal Version of ). ‣ B.2.1 Sample Efficiency ‣ B.2 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details in ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})=\mathrm{Cov}_{(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})\sim p,\,\pi\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\Pi_{k})}\left(-\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\mid\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})=\mathrm{Cov}_{(\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}})\sim p,\,\pi\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\Pi_{k})}\left(-\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\mid\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to verify that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}_{k}=\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}_{k}=\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Rewrite <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and we get that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[-\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[-\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E6Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[-\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[-\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E6Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}-\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}-\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\int_{\Omega^{k}}\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\cdot p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\int_{\Omega^{k}}\frac{\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}{q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})}\cdot p(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\int_{\Omega^{k}}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\int_{\Omega^{k}}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Due to the assumption <math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta^{*}}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta^{*}}=p</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\int_{\Omega^{k}}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}1\right]=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}\int_{\Omega^{k}}q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}1\right]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combined with <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2.1 Sample Efficiency ‣ B.2 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details in ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we can get that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}L_{k}(\theta^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Now rewrite the right-hand side of <a href="#A2.E5" title="In Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2.1 Sample Efficiency ‣ B.2 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details in ‣ LimiX: Unleashing Structured-Data Modeling Capability for Generalist Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{aligned} &amp;\,\mathrm{Cov}\left(-\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\mid\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\right)\\
=&amp;\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}\right]\\
&amp;\,-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]^{\top}\end{aligned}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>π</mi><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mtext>te</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mtext>ct</mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned} &amp;\,\mathrm{Cov}\left(-\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}\mid\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}}\right)\right)\\
=&amp;\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)\left(\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right)^{\top}\right]\\
&amp;\,-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}},\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}},\pi}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log q_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{\pi}|\mathbf{X}^{\text{te}}_{-\pi},\mathbf{X}^{\text{ct}})\right]^{\top}\end{aligned}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
